  "details": "Sometimes a Quest Asset (whether it be an avatar or world) fails to upload properly and no indication of such error is displayed to the creator. The SDK simply indicates a successful upload\n\nBelow is the image all Quest users will see displayed above the user if the asset is an avatar. \nFor worlds, the Quest user will be directed back to their homeworld.\n\nThis is especially an issue for creators who do not own a Quest to test on, where the only indication will have to come from a Quest user unable to load the asset and the user must be aware it is Quest compatible.\nAll Quest users will experience this with avatars, I do not know about worlds since I have personally not uploaded a Quest compatible world asset. \nThe work around that works is to simply reupload the asset until any quest user is able to use or view the asset.",
